{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487476-1st-ed-sunnikuse-and-gangrel-flaw-question","id":487476,"title":"1st ed - Sunnikuse and Gangrel Flaw Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-21T12:00:46-07:00","id":487476,"title":"1st ed - Sunnikuse and Gangrel Flaw Question","content":"Quick question (had no luck with a search) - In first edition requiem, does the gangrel flaw affect the first and fifth levels of the Bohagande Sunnikuse discipline, seeing as they are based on wits and intelligence pools.<br /> <br /> Many thanks for info or pointers to where this is discussed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","name":"Silvercat18","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4104_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T13:44:23-07:00","id":487587,"title":"","content":"Unless it explicitly states otherwise, I would assume it does.<br /> <br /> But that's dumb, in my opinion, so I wouldn't play it like that in practice. Talk it over with your ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T14:07:02-07:00","id":487623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487476-1st-ed-sunnikuse-and-gangrel-flaw-question?p=487587#post487587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it explicitly states otherwise, I would assume it does.<br /> <br /> But that's dumb, in my opinion, so I wouldn't play it like that in practice. Talk it over with your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm, it did strike me as puzzling that almost half the discipline would have been affected in this way, especially as its a bloodline discipline. I have certainly seen it mentioned as a popular choice, so I was hoping this would have come up somewhere.<br /> <br /> Additionally, as the fifth rank gives 8 or 9 again....that too is problematic for gangrel as their innate flaw can conflict with that....but it is never mentioned that it does. Technically, to give a 9 again to a character who does not have ten again in an ability gives them, I believe, ten again rather than 9 again....making up somewhat for the loss, but being watered down a step. If it just flat out replaces the flaw then that would be very interesting indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","user":"Silvercat18","date":". 04-21-2015, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","name":"Silvercat18","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4104_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T14:59:37-07:00","id":487675,"title":"","content":"I think the rule was that the flaw didn't apply to discipline usage. (see nosferatu and the very-much-social-based Nightmare)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:09:21-07:00","id":487680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487476-1st-ed-sunnikuse-and-gangrel-flaw-question?p=487675#post487675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the rule was that the flaw didn't apply to discipline usage. (see nosferatu and the very-much-social-based Nightmare)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm, that's what I am thinking, though I had some doubt on the issue as the gangrel flaw applies to Theban sorcery and the nosferatu one is mention not to apply to cruac. I`m unsure if these are even considered disciplines though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","name":"Silvercat18","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4104_2.png","title":"Member","rank"